{
  "outcome": "patch",
  "candidate_reviews": {
    "C001": {
      "decision": "edit",
      "reason": "The `VehicleTelemetry.encode` call must convert meters per second to kilometers per hour (multiply by 3.6) as per intended_behavior. The field name in the protobuf schema has changed from `speed_mps` to `speed_kph`, but the runtime logic must scale the input value before encoding."
    },
    "C002": {
      "decision": "edit",
      "reason": "The decoded output fields must reflect the new unit (`speed_kph`) and include the scaled value (multiplied by 3.6) for JSON observation, as per intended_behavior."
    },
    "C003": {
      "decision": "edit",
      "reason": "The speeding threshold check must use the scaled value (>108.0 km/h instead of >30.0 m/s) and expose the decoded `speed_kph` field in JSON output."
    }
  },
  "edits": [
    {
      "before": "    const sample = VehicleTelemetry.encode({ vehicleId: request.vehicle_id, speedMps: request.speed }).finish();\n",
      "after": "    const sample = VehicleTelemetry.encode({ vehicleId: request.vehicle_id, speedKph: request.speed * 3.6 }).finish();\n"
    },
    {
      "before": "    const fields = { vehicle_id: entity.vehicleId, speed_mps: entity.speedMps };\n",
      "after": "    const fields = { vehicle_id: entity.vehicleId, speed_kph: entity.speedKph };\n"
    },
    {
      "before": "    return { fields, speeding: entity.speedMps > 30.0, constructed_payload: Buffer.from(sample).toString(\"base64\") };\n",
      "after": "    return { fields, speeding: entity.speedKph > 108.0, constructed_payload: Buffer.from(sample).toString(\"base64\") };\n"
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The protobuf schema change requires runtime adjustments to handle the unit conversion (m/s → km/h) and reflect the new field name (`speed_kph`). The intended_behavior specifies scaling input values by 3.6 before serialization, using a strict threshold of >108.0 km/h for speeding decisions, and exposing exact decoded float32 values as JSON numbers. All edits align with these requirements while preserving wire format (float32) and entity IDs.",
  "confidence": 1.0,
  "assumptions": [
    "The protobuf `VehicleTelemetry` generated bindings correctly expose `speedKph` as a float32 field after the schema update.",
    "JSON output must use camelCase (`speed_kph`) for consistency with the new protobuf field name, despite the original snake_case in the source context."
  ]
}
